      howToRun: 'Ask the blameless-loss question cold — a tree on a fence, nobody at fault — and let the room argue for two minutes before saying that the storm did not decide it. Read Exodus 22:10-13 as a sequence and have somebody state the pattern out loud. Then read Genesis 31:38-40 straight through without interruption; it lands better whole. Spend the back half on the documents: everybody who brought a page finds the loss-bearing sentence, reads it aloud, and translates it into the three-in-the-morning version. Send home the longhand copy exercise for anyone who came empty-handed.',
