      howToRun: 'Open by asking what people actually think when they hear about somebody else’s disaster, and let it be honest. Read Luke 13:1-5 whole, once, without comment. Then go back and ask why Jesus added the tower; wait for the room to find the loophole He is closing. Read 3 and 5 aloud consecutively to make the repetition audible. Spend real time on both errors, and give each one a face — the neighbourhood deciding about a burned-out family, and a comfortable room hearing that the eighteen were unlucky and nothing more. Close with the written sentence, said plainly, and make the pairing offer for anyone still raw. Collect nothing and do not ask anyone to read theirs out.',
